.TH "mbedded\-cbor" "3" "2026-11-05" "mbedded\-cbor 0.9.0" "mbedded\-cbor"
.SH NAME
mbedded\-cbor \- a header\-only C++ library for CBOR (RFC 8949)
.SH DESCRIPTION
mbedded\-cbor is a header\-only C++ library for CBOR (RFC 8949).
.SS Highlights
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Fast.\f[R] \f[CR]cbor::schema\f[R] reads one field of the carsales
message of 1000 cars in 11.6 ns.
FlatBuffers with its Verifier takes 34.6 µs and Cap\(aqn Proto 144 ns.
Every library checks its input.
AMD Ryzen 9 5950X, g++ 16.2 \f[CR]\-O2 \-march=native\f[R], median of 7
runs: the run and its context.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Standard CBOR.\f[R] Every message that the library writes is
standard CBOR, and every other CBOR decoder reads it.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Safe on foreign input.\f[R] Bad input comes back as a
\f[CR]cbor::error\f[R] value.
No read goes outside the message.
Nesting depth, string length and element count are constants of the
build.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]JSONPath at compile time.\f[R] The compiler checks the path in
\f[CR]at_path<\(dq$.user.id\(dq>\f[R].
A path also takes CBOR keys that are not text, goes through tags and
reads typed arrays: path.
.SS Classes
.SS lazy
Use it for a message whose shape you learn while you read it.
.SS path
Use it for one value whose path you know.
.SS item
Use it for a tree that lives on after the bytes are gone, and CBOR
written item by item.
.SS structs
Use it for CBOR that any program wrote, read into the members of a
struct.
.SS schema
Use it for messages that your own programs write and read.
.SS ref
Use it for a result that points into the message and stays valid.
.SS tools
Use it for the end of an item, many items in a row, an item as text.
.SS errors
Use it for the reason why a call failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
cbor::lazy(3), cbor::at_path(3), cbor::item(3), cbor::structs(3), cbor::schema(3), cbor::ref(3), cbor::item_size(3), cbor::sequence(3), cbor::sequence_reader(3), cbor::diagnostic_notation(3), cbor::error(3)
